    <string name="migration_guide_title">Transferring Saves from Lemuroid</string>
    <string name="migration_guide_intro">Because Lemuroid and Omnidroid use the same save formats, all your in-game battery saves (.srm) and save states (.state) can be transferred seamlessly.\n\nOn modern Android (Android 11+), Android restricts apps from directly reading each other\'s internal data folders. Here are the easiest ways to move your saves:</string>
    <string name="migration_guide_method1_title">Method 1: Connect via USB to PC (Recommended)</string>
    <string name="migration_guide_method1_body">1. Connect your device to a computer via USB in File Transfer (MTP) mode.\n2. On your computer, open: Android/data/com.swordfish.lemuroid/files/\n3. Copy the \"saves\" and \"states\" folders.\n4. Paste them directly into: Android/data/com.omnidroid/files/\n5. Reopen Omnidroid and resume playing!</string>
    <string name="migration_guide_method2_title">Method 2: Using an On-Device File Manager</string>
    <string name="migration_guide_method2_body">1. Using a file manager that supports Android/data (such as ZArchiver or FV File Explorer with Shizuku), navigate to Android/data/com.swordfish.lemuroid/files/.\n2. Copy the \"saves\" or \"states\" folder to your \"Downloads\" or \"Documents\" folder (or compress them into a .zip).\n3. In Omnidroid, return here and tap \"Import from folder\" (or \"Import backup\") and select the copied folder/zip.</string>
    <string name="migration_guide_method3_title">Method 3: Direct 1-Tap Migration</string>
    <string name="migration_guide_method3_body">On Android 10 or older, rooted devices, and dedicated gaming handhelds (such as Retroid, Odin, or Anbernic), Omnidroid can detect Lemuroid directly. When detected, the 1-tap \"Migrate from Lemuroid\" button appears above automatically!</string>
